before diagnosis:
At 100000 msg/s, k=8, count=500000, sender emitted fec_parity_sent=401548 with fec_closed_by_timeout=390778. Expected full generations are about 500000 / 8 = 62500. The p50 inter-frame interval was 9953 ns and p99 was 33010 ns, so the FEC stage was generally being fed near the nominal 10 us cadence and should have reached k in about 80 us.

root cause:
The timeout was applied incorrectly. The sender closed a partial generation in the kEmpty branch on any transient empty shm read, without checking fec_timeout_ns. Since the producer is rate-limited, the ring is commonly empty between nominal 10 us arrivals. Those empties were counted as timeout closures even though 200 us had not elapsed. This is case (a), timeout applied incorrectly. Evidence: after removing that unconditional kEmpty close, 100k parity fell near sent / 8 and closed_by_k dominated.

