summary table after fix:
rate,count,sent,parity,closed_by_k,closed_by_timeout,arrival_p50_ns,arrival_p99_ns,data_bytes,parity_bytes,overhead_pct
100000,500000,494247,61993,61568,425,2559,14027,166058160,36801570,22.161856
300000,500000,120984,15185,15067,118,2480,13287,40599168,9002994,22.175316

interpretation:
100000: parity is now close to sent / 8. 494247 / 8 = 61780.875; observed parity=61993. Remaining timeout closures=425, explained by occasional long inter-frame stalls shown by max interval 76337519 ns.
300000: sender was starved/lapped under WSL2 loopback. It sent only 120984 of requested 500000 and lapped 2681 times. Despite starvation, parity is still close to sent / 8: 120984 / 8 = 15123; observed parity=15185.

parity bytes / data bytes:
100000 fixed: 36801570 / 166058160 * 100 = 22.161856%.
300000 fixed: 9002994 / 40599168 * 100 = 22.175316%.

not tuned:
--fec-timeout-us stayed 200. The fix changed when the existing timeout is applied, not the timeout value.
